The provider files above are required imports. Wrapping your application is optional; standalone components respect the system motion preference. To control a subtree, wrap it once:

```tsx
import { CadenceProvider } from "@/components/cadence/lib/provider";

export function MotionRoot({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return <CadenceProvider mode="full">{children}</CadenceProvider>;
}
```

Copy every file in the target list, including every shared `lib/` file.
Keep the mirrored `cadence/` tree, relative imports and `"use client"` directives
intact. The popup, backdrop, title and description are driven by the shared
presence, geometry, text, number and colour controllers, but the provider imports
still require `motion`. The provider files are required; wrapping your
application in `CadenceProvider` is optional.

Complete the base theme setup linked above, including Cadence's easing tokens,
and ensure Tailwind scans the copied files. There is no additional
Drawer-specific CSS or asset in these payloads. Each portalled popup, backdrop
and owned display resolves its own motion clock, including provider `timeScale`:
full plays the popup edge flight, the backdrop opacity, the measured content
height, the changed title/description runs and the scoped paint; reduced keeps
short opacity and colour feedback only; and none settles every target on the
first frame. Direct finger tracking remains in all three modes. Without a
wrapper, Drawer follows the system motion preference; a nested full scope still
respects the system reduced-motion preference.

