import { useId, useState } from "react";
import { Button } from "@/components/cadence/button";
import {
  Drawer,
  DrawerClose,
  DrawerContent,
  DrawerDescription,
  DrawerFooter,
  DrawerHeader,
  DrawerTitle,
  DrawerTrigger,
} from "@/components/cadence/drawer";
import { Field, FieldGroup, FieldLabel } from "@/components/cadence/field";
import { Input } from "@/components/cadence/input";

export function ControlledDrawer() {
  const id = useId();
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);
  const [draft, setDraft] = useState("Read later");
  const [saved, setSaved] = useState("Read later");
  return (
    <div className="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <Drawer open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen} showSwipeHandle>
        <DrawerTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Edit destination</DrawerTrigger>
        <DrawerContent>
          <DrawerHeader>
            <DrawerTitle>Destination label</DrawerTitle>
            <DrawerDescription>Rename this local example destination.</DrawerDescription>
          </DrawerHeader>
          <form
            className="flex flex-col gap-4 pt-4"
            onSubmit={(event) => {
              event.preventDefault();
              setSaved(draft);
              setOpen(false);
            }}
          >
            <FieldGroup>
              <Field>
                <FieldLabel htmlFor={id}>Destination draft</FieldLabel>
                <Input id={id} value={draft} onValueChange={setDraft} />
              </Field>
            </FieldGroup>
            <DrawerFooter>
              <DrawerClose render={<Button type="button" variant="outline" />}>Cancel</DrawerClose>
              <Button type="submit">Save destination</Button>
            </DrawerFooter>
          </form>
        </DrawerContent>
      </Drawer>
      <p role="status" className="text-sm">
        Saved: {saved}
      </p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Explicit motion scopes

Ordinary drawers inherit the header. This example alone fixes none and nests a full override, subject to the OS preference. Direct finger tracking remains in every mode; none removes the authored enter, exit and release duration.

<ComponentExample name="without-motion" />

```tsx
"use client";

import { Button } from "@/components/cadence/button";
import {
  Drawer,
  DrawerClose,
  DrawerContent,
  DrawerDescription,
  DrawerFooter,
  DrawerHeader,
  DrawerTitle,
  DrawerTrigger,
} from "@/components/cadence/drawer";
import { CadenceProvider } from "@/components/cadence/lib/provider";

export function DrawerMotionScopes() {
  return (
    <CadenceProvider mode="none">
      <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Drawer showSwipeHandle>
          <DrawerTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Open without motion</DrawerTrigger>
          <DrawerContent data-testid="initial-none">
            <DrawerHeader>
              <DrawerTitle>Immediate drawer</DrawerTitle>
              <DrawerDescription>No authored transition.</DrawerDescription>
            </DrawerHeader>
            <DrawerFooter>
              <DrawerClose render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Close</DrawerClose>
            </DrawerFooter>
          </DrawerContent>
        </Drawer>
        <CadenceProvider mode="full">
          <Drawer showSwipeHandle>
            <DrawerTrigger render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Open nested full</DrawerTrigger>
            <DrawerContent data-testid="nested-full">
              <DrawerHeader>
                <DrawerTitle>Nested full drawer</DrawerTitle>
                <DrawerDescription>The OS preference still wins.</DrawerDescription>
              </DrawerHeader>
              <DrawerFooter>
                <DrawerClose render={<Button variant="outline" />}>Close</DrawerClose>
              </DrawerFooter>
            </DrawerContent>
          </Drawer>
        </CadenceProvider>
      </div>
    </CadenceProvider>
  );
}
```

## When to use

- A short task opened from the bottom of the screen, where the thumb is: move to, share, quick actions.
- A list or explanation that the page behind should stay visible for — a bottom sheet covers the bottom,
  not the context.
- A panel the user expects to swipe away, because that is how sheets behave on touch devices.

## When not to use

- A decision that must be answered. Use `alert-dialog`; a drawer can be dragged shut.
- A hint on a control. Use `tooltip` or `hover-card`.
- A long multi-step flow. Use a page or a `sheet` with a footer; dragging half-way through a form is a
  worse experience than a full surface.

## API

| Part | Props | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Drawer` | `open`, `defaultOpen`, `onOpenChange`, `modal`, `snapPoints`, `swipeDirection`, `showSwipeHandle` | `showSwipeHandle` is additive; `swipeDirection` defaults to `"down"` and `modal` to `true`. |
| `DrawerTrigger` | native button props, `render` | Opens the drawer. |
| `DrawerContent` | `overlayClassName`, `overlayStyle`, `render`, `className`, `style` | Renders portal, overlay (when modal), viewport, popup, and content. The overlay props hook paint only the backdrop. |
| `DrawerOverlay` | `className`, `style` | Only needed when replacing `DrawerContent`. |
| `DrawerSwipeHandle` | `className` | The handle; rendered for you when `showSwipeHandle` is set. |
| `DrawerClose` | native button props, `render` | Closes the drawer. |
| `DrawerHeader` / `DrawerFooter` | `className` | Stacking and spacing only. |
| `DrawerTitle` | `className`, `style` | Required accessible name. A direct string changes by grapheme and a direct number rolls its digits. |
| `DrawerDescription` | `className`, `style` | Supporting text. Accepts the same direct string and quantity display behavior as the title. |

## Motion contract

Authored intensity is **medium**: Drawer owns its popup edge flight, the independently owned backdrop opacity, the
popup's measured content height, scoped paint and owned title/description display while Base UI keeps the swipe, snap
and release gesture.

Each portal surface resolves its own mode and token clock. A nested full scope restores timing inside none (subject to
the system preference). Base parts accept `className(state)` and `style(state)`; caller values merge last. Live
reduced drops the edge flight, the measured height and the text/number replacement and keeps a short opacity/colour
feedback; none settles every target on the first frame and cancels the running writer.

| Phase | Properties | Token | Interruptible |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| enter | popup `opacity 0 → 1` plus a `transform` translation from its own edge extent | `popup.anchored/one-shot` · `duration.slow` | yes, a reversal continues from the current paint |
| backdrop enter | backdrop `opacity 0 → 1` on its own host, sharing the native swipe-progress channel | `data.transition/one-shot` · `duration.base` | yes, a direct swipe takes over the same channel |
| exit | popup `opacity → 0` and `transform` back off its edge; backdrop `opacity → 0` | `exit.fade/one-shot` · popup `duration.base` / backdrop `duration.fast` | yes (reopen mid-exit) |
| content revision | clamped measured popup block size while open and no snap height is active | `geometry.resize/measured` · `spring.sizePanel` | yes, retargets from the current size |
| title / description text | changed graphemes only, no stagger | `text.change/changed-runs` | yes, the newest diff replaces the old target |
| direct numeric title / description quantity | changed place values only | `number.roll/reels` | yes, retargets the current reel |
| backdrop / title / description paint | scoped surface or foreground colour; focus or an unprovable palette is immediate | `state.color/css-transition` | yes, latest committed colour |
| swipe, snap, release and configure | Base UI's own inline transform, snap offsets and release trajectory | Base UI engine (no authored recipe) | yes, it is the gesture |

The travel distance is the popup's own rendered height or width, expressed as a percentage of that box, so each edge
enters from exactly off its edge without a distance token per direction. Placement is the native snap offset on
`translate`; the drag and the authored entrance share `transform` but never at the same time, because pointer input
settles the authored envelope first. A live `swipeDirection` change settles the obsolete envelope and places the new
edge immediately instead of flying across the viewport. Only the block axis is measured, and only while the drawer is
open and its height is not the native snap transaction's; a snap-point drawer settles an explicit height change
natively rather than writing a second one.

The popup's supplied paint settles immediately: its single CSS transition family is Base UI's own swipe and release
channel, and an authored colour clock there would have to displace that native release. The backdrop, title and
description keep their own colour owners.

Focus, pointer or key activation inside an entering popup settles that popup immediately while the independently owned
backdrop may continue. Base UI retains focus, portal, modality and completion ownership, including
`preventUnmountOnClose`.

## Keyboard interactions

| Keys | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Tab / Shift+Tab | Cycles focus inside a modal drawer. |
| Escape | Closes the drawer and returns focus to the trigger. |
| Enter / Space | Activates the focused control. |

## Accessibility

- Base UI provides `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, `aria-labelledby` / `aria-describedby`, focus
  trapping, focus return, scroll lock, and Escape handling while the drawer is modal.
- `DrawerTitle` is required: a drawer without an accessible name is invalid.
- The swipe handle is `aria-hidden="true"` and is never the only way out. A user who cannot drag gets
  the close controls, Escape, and the overlay press (for a modal drawer).
- The content region scrolls on its own (`overflow-y-auto`), so a long list inside the sheet does not
  move the page behind it.

## Responsive behavior

The default sheet sits at the bottom, spans the width, and caps its height at `calc(100dvh - 3rem)` so a
strip of the page stays visible. `swipeDirection="left"` / `"right"` becomes a side panel at `w-3/4`,
capped at `max-w-sm` from `sm` up. Snap points change the resting height without changing any of that
geometry.

## Performance

- The drag writes CSS variables and Base UI's own inline `transform`; it never touches layout or React state per
  frame, and the authored entrance has settled before the gesture starts.
- The backdrop opacity is a `calc()` on the same swipe-progress variable, so the page behind dims as the drawer moves
  without a second animation.
- Entry and exit animate `transform` and `opacity` only. The measured content revision is one clamped block-size
  transaction at a committed content revision, and changed text and numeric reels are bounded to the changed runs.
- Nothing is measured during render. The measured owner reads the natural height after releasing its own size
  overlay, so a child's interpolated box is never reused as a fresh target.

## Notes for AI

- Use `drawer` for a short touch-first task from the bottom edge; use `sheet` for a side panel that
  holds a form, and `alert-dialog` when the answer must be deliberate.
- Always render `DrawerTitle`. `DrawerDescription` is the second line of the announcement.
- Never make the swipe the only dismissal: keep a `DrawerClose`, and let Escape work.
- For a list of actions, each row is a `DrawerClose` so choosing one closes the sheet.
